    "https://delhi.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204648": {
      "title": "Plumber & Steamfitter -Trades Specialist",
      "description": "SUNY Delhi\nJob Posting: Plumber & Steamfitter -Trades Specialist SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: Plumber & Steamfitter -Trades Specialist Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Plumber & Steamfitter -Trades Specialist Category: Civil Service - CSEA Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Facilities Locations: Delhi, NY Posted: Sep 10, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 355017 Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $50,425.00 - $50,425.00 Position ID: 204648 Share About SUNY Delhi: SUNY Delhi is leading the way with cutting-edge programs, including Applied Technology (Architecture, Mechatronics, Construction trades, etc.), Veterinary Science, Nursing, Sustainability, Culinary Arts, Liberal Arts, NCAA Division III athletics, etc.  We are fueled by our passion to become a leader in the higher education space by our commitment to excellence, celebrating diversity, and including faculty, staff and students from all walks of life!  Check out our 60+ award-winning Majors/Programs here . While credentials and technical skills are required, SUNY Delhi values those who are committed to continuous learning/growth, work well independently as well as with a team, and are curious, analytical, and problem-solvers.  Being a champion for our approximately 2,600 students and the SUNY Delhi mission is essential! If you share these values, please consider applying to become part of our team! Located in the beautiful Catskill Mountains with breathtaking views, you may find more information about Delhi, New York, and the surrounding area here. The College offers an outdoor education center, state-of-the-art fitness center, indoor pool, golf simulator, and an 18-hole golf course!  Find a virtual tour of our campus here . See where we rank on US News . Job Description: SUNY Delhi seeks a dynamic, forward-thinking Trades Specialist Plumber & Steamfitter to join the Facilities Department in the Plumbing Shop . SUNY Delhi prides itself on being a welcoming college community for all. Diversity, equity, and inclusiveness are integral components of the highest quality academic programs and the strongest campus climate. The college seeks a wide range of applicants for its positions so that inclusive excellence will be affirmed. This facilities Plumbing Shop position is responsible for the installation, repair, and maintenance of plumbing related work in all campus buildings including six residence halls, as well as, exterior underground piping systems. This position will perform journey-level plumbing work including installation, alteration, and repair of pipes, fittings, fixtures, equipment, and drainage systems in accordance to specifications, and NY State Plumbing Code. The Plumbing Shop is responsible for distribution systems for water, septic, and storm water. This position will supervise others in area of plumbing. Responsibilities include but are not limited to: Repairs, maintains, and installs plumbing fixtures and appliances such as sinks, shower baths, toilets, drinking fountains, dishwashers, valves including pneumatic controls, gas and water meters, gas hot water heaters, and other gas appliances, various steam equipment used in kitchens and food service, water pumps, and hydrotherapy equipment. Assess malfunction or breakdown of equipment, working with end user to resolve issues, using testing equipment such as pressure and vacuum gauge to assist with troubleshooting. Follow technical manuals, codes, diagrams, and previous experience to plan new work or repairs to existing equipment. Reviews building plans and working drawings to determine work, and sequence of installation, locating and identifying pipes, connections and passages holes, as well as, cutting openings in floors and walls to accommodate pipes and fittings. Plans and lays out the installation, alteration, and repair of high- and low-pressure pipe systems that carry water, steam, air, or other liquids or gases consistent with specifications, plans, and plumbing codes. Makes necessary repairs or adjustments or directs others in performing such activities. Measure, cut, bend, and assemble pipes and fittings (metal and non-metal). Join piping by means of threaded, caulked, wiped, soldered, brazed, fused, or cemented joints. Tests pipe system for leaks by filling with liquid or air and reading pressure gauges. Replace existing fixtures in bathrooms, labs, and work areas. Clean drains, traps, sewage, and storm sewer lines. Maintains and repairs underground water sanitary, and storm sewage lines. Completes information on Work Order (WO) system, prioritizes WO's importance to fit campus need. From blueprints, or specifications may estimate labor, materials, tools, and equipment for assigned work. Use computer to research parts, and materials, obtaining quotes needed for ordering and completion work. Assigns work to Assistant Plumber, giving verbal or demonstrative instructions on proper plumbing techniques, and use of tools and equipment. Inspect work when completed. Requirements: Minimum Qualifications: Non-competitive: Four years of full-time experience in plumbing under a skilled tradesperson which would provide training equivalent to that given in a training, apprenticeship, or equivalent program, OR, an equivalent combination of experience and training gained by completion of technical courses in plumbing at a school, institute, or branch of the Armed Services; OR, Successful completion of the two-year Trades Specialist (Plumber & Steamfitter) traineeship or a two-year plumbing training, apprenticeship, or equivalent program* such as the New York State Civil Service Employees Association-Partnership Applied Skilled Trades Traineeship and Certificate Program. * Successful completion of the traineeship and the training program includes a total of 288 hours of trade-specific class room instruction, 45 hours of technical math course work, 45 hours of technical communications course work, and 15 hours of blueprint/schematic reading course work.  Course work must be completed with an average of \"C\" or better. Additionally, successful completion of the traineeship also includes 4,000 hours of on-the-job training. Additional Information: Status: Full-time, Permanent Negotiating Unit: 03 - Operational Services Unit (OSU) Salary:  $50,425, SG-12 Work Schedule:  6:00 am - 2:30 pm, 40 hrs/wk, Monday - Friday. The assignment may be made to include weekend and holiday work to meet the needs of the campus. Reports to: Plant Utilities Engineer 3 Location: SUNY Delhi This position offers full New York State CSEA , benefits, which are among the most comprehensive in the country. Click here for Information for Prospective Employees SUNY Delhi has a strong commitment to Affirmative Action and Cultural Diversity. The College welcomes responses from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities, and veterans. SUNY Delhi is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community for our students and employees. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final candidates being considered for employment. Any offer of employment is contingent on the successful completion of the background check. Although the vacancies are in the areas indicated, the appointing authority shall have the right to direct appropriate transfers and reassignments of employees to other areas. Application Instructions: SUNY Delhi is energized to lead the charge in developing a welcoming and intellectually diverse environment for all, a place where diversity, equity and success guide our achievement, scholarship, character and global citizenship. To apply please attach the following items and provide a short statement in your cover letter on your commitment to diversity and how you would incorporate it into this role. Cover Letter Resume Contact information for three professional references For full consideration please apply by September 25, 2026 and will remain posted until filled. SUNY Delhi is an AA/EOE employer. SUNY Delhi does not discriminate. All people with disabilities are encouraged to apply Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Your application will not be accepted if you require sponsorship to work in the United States. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
    },
    "https://delhi.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205162": {
      "title": "Resident Assistants (Spring 2027)",
      "description": "SUNY Delhi\nJob Posting: Resident Assistants (Spring 2027) SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: Resident Assistants (Spring 2027) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Resident Assistants (Spring 2027) Category: Active Student Jobs Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Residence Life Locations: Delhi, NY Posted: Sep 24, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Temporary Ref. No.: 356026 Position ID: 205162 Share About SUNY Delhi: SUNY Delhi, founded in 1913, is a student-centered college that offers specialized certificates, nationally-recognized associate degree programs, unique baccalaureate degrees and a master's degree in Nursing Education. A targeted expansion of baccalaureate programs through satellite campuses and on-line has led to a record enrollment of more than 3,400 students. A charter member of the State University of New York system, the college is also recognized for forming innovative partnerships that enhance regional economic growth, and for the college's commitment to civic engagement, applied learning, and service-learning. Located in the beautiful foothills of the Catskill Mountains, Delhi and the surrounding area offer outstanding recreational opportunities and small-town charm. Binghamton, the Capitol District and Metropolitan New York are easily accessible. SUNY Delhi was recognized in 2009, 2010 and 2015 as a \"Great College to Work for\" by the Chronicle of Higher Education. Job Description: The Resident Assistant (RA) is a member of the Office of Residence Life Staff, working in an assigned Residence Hall. The RA reports to and is supervised by the professional staff member assigned to the Residence Hall in which they work. Duties of Resident Assistants: Facilitate community development in residence halls. Enforce policies. Serve as a student leader for the Department of Residence Life. Assist the Residence Hall Director in managing the residence halls. Administrative duties Requirements: Minimum Requirements: Good judicial standing Minimum 2.5 cumulative GPA Additional Information: Job Benefits: Free single room $800 off meal plan, and an additional $100 a year up to $1000 $300 stipend Leadership development Transferable skills Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
    },
    "https://delhi.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205185": {
      "title": "Early Outreach Academic Advisor",
      "description": "SUNY Delhi\nJob Posting: Early Outreach Academic Advisor SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: Early Outreach Academic Advisor Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Early Outreach Academic Advisor Category: Staff - UUP Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Academic Affairs Locations: Delhi, NY Posted: Sep 25, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 355203 Position ID: 205185 Share About SUNY Delhi: Fast Facts about SUNY Delhi Job Description: Reporting to the Director of Academic Advisement & Student Success, the Early Outreach Academic Advisor serves as a key member of the student success team, leading proactive outreach and intervention efforts that support student persistence, retention, and degree completion. This position facilitates early alert initiatives, academic recovery efforts, and SUNY Reconnect advising while maintaining a student advising caseload. The Advisor develops and executes data-informed outreach strategies to identify and support students experiencing academic, financial, personal, or administrative barriers to success. Working collaboratively with Admissions, Financial Aid, the Registrar, faculty, academic schools, and student support services, this role helps students navigate transitions into, through, and back to college. The Advisor also serves as the campus liaison for the Academic Recovery Program , ensuring a consistent student experience and coordinating support for students seeking to regain good academic standing. In addition, the position provides advising and case management services for students participating in the SUNY Reconnect initiative and supports institutional Academic Momentum and student success efforts. Primary Responsibilities Coordinate and manage early alert systems and proactive student outreach initiatives. Provide case management and individualized support for at-risk students. Serve as the primary advisor for students participating in SUNY Reconnect and reentry/readmission programs. Develop and implement intervention strategies designed to increase student persistence and retention. Collaborate with Admissions to support students transitioning back to college and ensure a seamless reentry process. Serve as liaison for the Academic Recovery Program and coordinate support services with academic schools and campus partners. Monitor student progress and connect students with appropriate academic, financial, wellness, and support resources. Support Academic Momentum and other student success initiatives. Maintain an advising caseload and assist students in developing academic plans aligned with their educational and career goals. Interpret and communicate institutional policies, academic requirements, degree pathways, transfer regulations, and graduation requirements. Present workshops, seminars, and success programming related to academic achievement, registration, persistence, and student engagement. Refer students to campus resources including Counseling & Health Services, Academic Achievement Center, Career & Transfer Services, Financial Aid, and other support offices as appropriate. Participate in orientation, admissions events, Accepted Student Day programs, and other enrollment-related initiatives. Assist with registration support and outreach to incoming and continuing students. Maintain accurate student records and utilize advising technologies such as Degree Works, Banner, and early alert platforms. Teach First Year Experience (UNIV 100) and/or Student Success (UNIV 101) up to 4 credit hours per semester Contribute to assessment and continuous improvement efforts within Academic Advisement and Student Success. Foster collaborative relationships with students, faculty, staff, and administrators. Demonstrate effective time management, organization, and the ability to manage multiple priorities while meeting deadlines. Requirements: Bachelor's degree in psychology, education or related field Experience working with and advising college level students Excellent verbal, written and interpersonal communication skills as well as computer proficiency Preferred Qualifications: Advanced degree in related field Working knowledge of Banner System Working knowledge of degree evaluation system (Degree Works or similar product) Familiarity with financial aid guidelines and its impact on academic advisement Additional Information: Salary: Starting at $57,651 Work Schedule: Full-time, Mon - Fri 8:00 am - 4:00 pm, Schedule flexibility is required, including a rotating schedule of evening and weekend shifts based on operational needs Reports to: Director of Academic Advisement & Student Success This is a 12-month position Budget Title: Senior Staff Assistant, SL3 This position offers full New York State UUP (FT) ,  benefits which are among the most comprehensive in the country with an excellent fringe benefits package Click here for more Information for Prospective Employees SUNY Delhi has a strong commitment to Affirmative Action and Cultural Diversity. The College welcomes responses from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities and veterans. SUNY Delhi is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community for our students and employees. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final candidates being considered for employment. Any offer of employment is contingent on the successful completion of the background check. Application Instructions: SUNY Delhi is energized to lead the charge in developing a welcoming and intellectually diverse environment for all, a place where diversity, equity and success guide our achievement, scholarship, character and global citizenship. To apply please attach the following items and provide a short statement in your cover letter on your commitment to diversity and how you would incorporate it into this role. Cover Letter Resume Contact information for three professional references For full consideration please apply by October 25, 2026 and will remain posted until filled. SUNY Delhi is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, protected veteran status, disability or membership in any other class protected by Federal, State, or local law. Clery Statement Applicants interested in positions may access the Annual Security Report (ASR) for SUNY Delhi online. The ASR contains information on campus security policies and certain campus crime statistics. Crime statistics are reported in accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Applicants may request a hard copy of the ASR by contacting the SUNY Delhi University Police Department at 607-746-4700 Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
    },
    "https://delhi.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205178": {
      "title": "Supervising Janitor (NY HELPS)",
      "description": "SUNY Delhi\nJob Posting: Supervising Janitor (NY HELPS) SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: Supervising Janitor (NY HELPS) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Supervising Janitor (NY HELPS) Category: Civil Service - CSEA Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Facilities/Custodial Locations: Delhi, NY Posted: Oct 1, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Temporary Ref. No.: 356085 Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $49,841.00 - $49,841.00 Position ID: 205178 Share About SUNY Delhi: SUNY Delhi is an inclusive, student-centered campus that transforms student lives through hands-on learning, innovation, engaged faculty, and exceptional support services. A close-knit campus community set in the scenic foothills of the Catskill Mountains, Delhi is a leader within the SUNY system for applied learning and online programs that cater to a diverse student population of over 3,000 students in over 65 popular majors ranging from associate to master degrees.  SUNY Delhi employs approximately 550 full-time, and part-time faculty and staff to fulfill its mission of transforming lives. SUNY Delhi currently offers over 50 student clubs and organizations, as well as 19 NCAA Division III athletic teams. SUNY Delhi has received national accolades for affordability, online education programs, and outstanding student success. As the county seat for Delaware County, Delhi is a bustling village with eateries, shops, government offices, and more.  SUNY Delhi is an integral part of the community, doubling its population when college is in session.  The College offers an array of activities and programs throughout the year for faculty and staff, including a state-of-the-art fitness center, racquetball courts, indoor/outdoor tennis courts, track, basketball courts, indoor pool, sauna, golf simulator, and even an 18-hole golf course. SUNY Delhi employees enjoy unique perks which include access to a student-run restaurant, Community Dog Wash Days, on-campus Butcher Shop, Automotive Repair Shop, and free Professional Development Workshops offered twice a year to help faculty and staff learn innovative teaching skills, earn certificates, get valuable training, and explore new interests. Most employees come for a visit and stay for a lifetime. To learn more about SUNY Delhi, visit www.delhi.edu . Job Description: SUNY Delhi seeks a dynamic, forward thinking,, and engaging Supervising Janitor to join the Facilities/Custodial Department. SUNY Delhi prides itself on being a welcoming college community for all. Diversity, equity, and inclusiveness are integral components of the highest quality academic programs and the strongest campus climate. The college seeks a wide range of applicants for its positions so that inclusive excellence will be affirmed. As a Supervising Janitor, you would supervise a staff of Janitors and Cleaners and may be responsible for all cleaning activities for the entire campus. Incumbent will plan and schedule staff assignments and cleaning services, supervise the proper distribution and control of cleaning equipment and supplies, inspect buildings and assigned areas, and train new staff. May be required to prepare reports such as work activity, and supervise the arrangement of set-ups for special occasions. You would also interview and select staff, establish training standards and train new staff, resolve personnel problems, and evaluate work performance. Requirements: The successful candidate must be reachable for appointment on a present, permanent Civil Service-eligible list for Supervising Janitor; or NY-HELPS Must have two years of satisfactory full-time experience in the custodial care or cleaning of buildings. One year of the experience must have been at a supervisory level. Incumbent must be able to effectively supervise staff, read and follow instructions, and work as a collegial team member Must have a valid unrestricted NY State drivers license Additional Information: Full-time, may include weekends Status: Full-time, probationary CSEA -SG-11, OSU Starting Salary: $49,841 Reports to:  Custodial and Transportation Services Manager This position offers full New York State CSEA , benefits which are among the most comprehensive in the country with an excellent fringe benefits package Click here for Information for Prospective Employees SUNY Delhi has a strong commitment to Affirmative Action and Cultural Diversity. The College welcomes responses from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities and veterans. SUNY Delhi is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community for our students and employees. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final candidates being considered for employment. Any offer of employment is contingent on the successful completion of the background check. Although the vacancies are in the areas indicated, the appointing authority shall have the right to direct appropriate transfers and reassignments of employees to other areas. *For the duration of the NY HELPS Program, this title maybe filled via a non - competitive appointment, which means no examination is required but all candidates must meet the minimum qualifications of the title for which they apply. At this time, agencies may recruit and hire employees by making temporary appointments. In May 2024, if a temporary NY HELPS employee is satisfactorily performing in the position, the appointment will be changed from temporary pending Civil Service Commission Action to permanent non-competitive and the official probationary period will begin. At a future date (within one year of permanent appointment), it is expected employees hired under NY HELPS will have their non-competitive employment status converted to competitive status, without having to compete in an examination. Employees will then be afforded with all of the same rights and privileges of competitive class employees of New York State. While serving permanently in a NY HELPS title, employees may take part in any promotion examination for which they are qualified. The NY HELPS program for the state workforce expires on June 30, 2028. Application Instructions: To apply, please submit: Letter of interest Resume Contact information for three professional references For full consideration applications must be received by October 16, 2026. Position will remain open until filled . SUNY Delhi has a strong commitment to Affirmative Action and Cultural Diversity. The College welcomes responses from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities and veterans. SUNY Delhi is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community for our students and employees. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final candidates being considered for employment. Any offer of employment is contingent on the successful completion of the background check. If you need a disability-related accommodation, please contact nochevgn@delhi.edu Clery Statement Applicants interested in positions may access the Annual Security Report (ASR) for SUNY Delhi online. The ASR contains information on campus security policies and certain campus crime statistics. Crime statistics are reported in accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Applicants may request a hard copy of the ASR by contacting the SUNY Delhi University Police Department at 607-746-4700. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
    },
    "https://delhi.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=203639": {
      "title": "Janitor",
      "description": "SUNY Delhi\nJob Posting: Janitor - SG 7 SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: Janitor - SG 7 Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Janitor - SG 7 Category: Civil Service - CSEA Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Facilities/Transportation Locations: Delhi, NY Posted: Aug 13, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $38,235.00 - $38,235.00 Position ID: 203639 Share About SUNY Delhi: SUNY Delhi is leading the way with cutting-edge programs, including Applied Technology (Architecture, Mechatronics, Construction trades, etc.), Veterinary Science, Nursing, Sustainability, Culinary Arts, Liberal Arts, NCAA Division III athletics, etc. We are fueled by our passion to become a leader in the higher education space by our commitment to excellence, celebrating diversity, and including faculty, staff and students from all walks of life! Check out our 60+ award-winning Majors/Programs here https://www.delhi.edu/academics/majors-programs/index.php . While credentials and technical skills are required, SUNY Delhi values those who are committed to continuous learning/growth, work well independently as well as with a team, and are curious, analytical, and problem-solvers. Being a champion for our approximately 2,600 students and the SUNY Delhi mission https://www.delhi.edu/about/president-office/strategic-plan/index.php is essential! If you share these values, please consider applying to become part of our team! Located in the beautiful Catskill Mountains with breathtaking views, you may find more information about Delhi, New York, and the surrounding area here https://www.visitdelhiny.com/ . The College offers an outdoor education center, state-of-the-art fitness center, indoor pool, golf simulator, and an 18-hole golf course! Find a virtual tour of our campus here https://www.delhi.edu/admission/visit-delhi/index.php . See where we rank on US News https://www.usnews.com/best-colleges/suny-college-of-technology-delhi-2857 Job Description: Janitors perform a variety of routine manual tasks that require light, medium, and heavy physical effort in the cleaning and caring for an assigned area on campus that includes academic and office buildings, athletic facilities, a student and community center, student residence halls, a health center, and the adjacent grounds and sidewalks of various buildings. Janitors work independently, and as part of a work team, performing a wide range of specialized and routine cleaning of floors, windows, trash and recycling removal, and walls. Work requires cleaning specialized areas within buildings such as; office spaces, kitchens, common areas, lounges, laundry rooms, locker rooms, bathrooms, classrooms, and laboratories. Responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Using small hand tools to perform minor repairs. Performing a variety of custodial tasks including maintenance and repair work requiring basic maintenance abilities. Removing snow and ice, plus salting entranceways and walkways Overseeing and training cleaners. Receiving and responding to emails, and utilizing the SUNY Portal for Time and Attendance Record keeping. Requirements: Must be able to physically perform the tasks of the position Must be able to communicate effectively to obtain and convey information Must have a valid NYS Drivers License Additional Information: Full-Time, 40 hrs/wk Status: Probationary Class: CSEA, Operational Services Unit Salary: $38,235 - Salary Grade 7 Reports to: Custodial Operations Manager SUNY Delhi has a strong commitment to Affirmative Action and Cultural Diversity. The College welcomes responses from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities and veterans. SUNY Delhi is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community for our students and employees. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final candidates being considered for employment. Although the vacancy is in the area indicated, the appointing authority shall have the right to direct appropriate transfers and reassignments of employees to other areas. Application Instructions: SUNY Delhi is energized to lead the charge in developing a welcoming and intellectually diverse environment for all, a place where diversity, equity and success guide our achievement, scholarship, character and global citizenship. To apply please attach the following items and provide a short statement in your cover letter on your commitment to diversity and how you would incorporate it into this role. Resume Cover letter Contact information for three professional references For full consideration please apply by August 27, 2026. SUNY Delhi is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, protected veteran status, disability or membership in any other class protected by Federal, State, or local law. URL: State University of New York AT Delhi Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
    },
    "https://delhi.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205019": {
      "title": "ASSOCIATE DEAN",
      "description": "SUNY Delhi\nJob Posting: ASSOCIATE DEAN - Veterinary Science SUNY Delhi \n\tJob Posting: ASSOCIATE DEAN - Veterinary Science Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details ASSOCIATE DEAN - Veterinary Science Category: Administration Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Applied Professions Locations: Delhi, NY Posted: Oct 5, 2026 Closes: Oct 30, 2026 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Full-time Ref. No.: 351999 Salary Type: Annually Salary Range: $90,000.00 - $90,000.00 Position ID: 205019 Share About SUNY Delhi: SUNY Delhi is leading the way with cutting-edge programs, including Applied Technology (Architecture, Mechatronics, Construction trades, etc.), Veterinary Science, Nursing, Sustainability, Culinary Arts, Liberal Arts, NCAA Division III athletics, etc.  We are fueled by our passion to become a leader in the higher education space by our commitment to excellence, celebrating diversity, and including faculty, staff and students from all walks of life!  Check out our 60+ award-winning Majors/Programs here . While credentials and technical skills are required, SUNY Delhi values those who are committed to continuous learning/growth, work well independently as well as with a team, and are curious, analytical, and problem-solvers.  Being a champion for our approximately 2,600 students and the SUNY Delhi mission is essential! If you share these values, please consider applying to become part of our team! Located in the beautiful Catskill Mountains with breathtaking views, you may find more information about Delhi, New York, and the surrounding area here . The College offers an outdoor education center, state-of-the-art fitness center, indoor pool, golf simulator, and an 18-hole golf course!  Find a virtual tour of our campus here . See where we rank on US News Job Description: Position Duties & Responsibilities Key Responsibilities of this role are: Governance, Leadership and Administration: Provides strategic leadership and day-to-day administrative oversight for veterinary science programs (on campus and online), ensuring alignment with college mission, policies, and shared governance. Leads departmental and program meetings; coordinates committee work supporting academic quality and accreditation readiness. Organizes direct reports under his/her supervision to promote broad-based participation and equitable apportionment of program essential functions and initiatives. Represents the School of Veterinary Science at internal and external meetings; serves on campus-wide committees and cultivates productive partnerships/agreements with institutional offices and external stakeholders. Serves in the Dean's absence, as assigned by the Provost, and/or assumes program director coverage and/or teaching responsibilities when coverage is not available. Provides leadership in tasks and functions as identified by the dean. Budget and Resource Oversight: Assists the Dean in developing the annual Unit Plan and multi-year program initiatives, with attention to resource sufficiency and efficiency for curriculum delivery and clinical training. Supports budgeting processes; monitors expenditures; approves purchase orders and payroll as assigned; tracks variances and implements corrective actions as needed. Collaborates with the Dean on college foundation and grant opportunities to strengthen instructional, clinical, and student support capacity Accreditation and Compliance: Partners with appropriate campus offices and program personnel to ensure teaching and clinical environments are safe, appropriately equipped, and supportive of program needs, including biosecurity and animal welfare requirements. Oversees direct reports in ensuring all compliance reporting is appropriately prepared and submitted with college, regulatory, and accrediting offices/agencies. Participates with direct reports in facility and animal welfare inspections as appropriate. Participates in periodic space and equipment reviews; prioritizes instructional and clinical equipment requests to sustain educational quality and compliance. Ensures veterinary science programs engage in appropriate data collection/analysis to support accreditation reporting. Prepares annual accreditation reports. Prepares self-study documents and oversees site visit readiness processes in consultation with the Provost's Office. Clinical Oversight: Provides oversight to staff and faculty to ensure that programs provide adequate case exposure, species mix, and supervised clinical learning opportunities. Ensures the program has appropriate processes and procedures in place to monitor off-campus site agreements, quality assurance, and documentation. Information Resources: Collaborates with campus library and IT to support appropriate access to veterinary resources and instructional technologies. Student Support: Addresses student concerns as needed. Supports advising, retention, and progression initiatives. Ensures programs operate within college requirements concerning the protection and confidentiality of student records (i.e., FERPA). 7. Admissions: Collaborates with all applicable college offices to ensure admissions processes are transparent, clear, and equitable. Coordinates programs' participation in college Open House events, new student events, student orientations, and other recruitment efforts as needed. Faculty and Staff: Under the direction of the dean, supports the recruitment, onboarding, and mentorship efforts of new veterinary sciences full-time and adjunct faculty. Under the direction of the Dean, conducts classroom observations of full-time and adjunct faculty in alignment with the collective bargaining agreement and accreditation expectations and supports the professional development of faculty. Supports faculty scholarship as appropriate. Establishes appropriate work expectations and responsibilities for program staff in concert with staff workload expectations and all applicable collective bargaining agreements. Under the direction of the dean, generates faculty workload assignments each semester based on program needs, student learning needs, and in alignment with college and collective bargaining requirements. Curriculum, Program Assessment, and Course Scheduling Provides leadership and guidance to faculty in the development of curriculum, curriculum mapping, and curriculum delivery that aligns with accreditation requirements, student learning needs, and the college's strategic plan. Ensures that the regular assessment of veterinary science programs occurs and leads continuous improvement efforts based on assessment data Develops the course schedule for all veterinary science programs and collaborates with the dean on ensuring program required general education courses are accessible to veterinary science students. Ensures full-time faculty teaching loads, full-time faculty extra service, and adjunct assignments meet program needs and are assigned in concert with all applicable college, SUNY policies, and collective bargaining agreements. Oversees school secretary in the data entry of course schedules, workload contracts, and student registrations/de-registrations Requirements: Education/Licensure: Unencumbered DVN license in the State of New York or acquisition of a NYS DVM license within six (6) months of hire; or, Ph.D. in Veterinary Science with an unencumbered New York State veterinary technician license or willingness to obtain a veterinary technician license within six (6) months of hire. Experience: Successful teaching experience Academic administrative experience Skills: Ability to relate fairly and objectively with all employees, students, and community members. Understanding of the various conceptual and methodological features of the initiatives offered within Academic Affairs, and a sense of how these initiatives are integrated in the pursuit of knowledge and in the promotion of learning Understanding of and ability to clearly communicate the aims and purposes of the academic initiatives Knowledge to effectively manage and lead a complex academic school with specialized labs Working knowledge of developing and administering a budget Ability to motivate staff to perform well, to improve, and to participate in divisional and college affairs Leadership abilities Preferred Qualifications Education: Certification in curriculum development and online learning technologies Experience: Work experience in overseeing or managing animal husbandry programs Additional Information: Starting and ending dates: As Soon As Possible Salary:  $90,000/Annual Obligation: Calendar Year, 12 months Reports to: Dean of College of Health, Liberal Arts and Sciences Budget Title:  Associate Dean, This position offers full New York State Management Confidential benefits which are among the most comprehensive in the country with an excellent fringe benefits package Click here for more Information for Prospective Employees SUNY Delhi has a strong commitment to Affirmative Action and Cultural Diversity. The College welcomes responses from women, minorities, individuals with disabilities and veterans. SUNY Delhi is committed to providing a safe and productive learning and living community for our students and employees. To achieve that goal, we conduct background investigations for all final candidates being considered for employment. Any offer of employment is contingent on the successful completion of the background check. If you need a disability-related accommodation, please contact nochevgn@delhi.edu Clery Statement Applicants interested in positions may access the Annual Security Report (ASR) for SUNY Delhi online. The ASR contains information on campus security policies and certain campus crime statistics. Crime statistics are reported in accordance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. Applicants may request a hard copy of the ASR by contacting the SUNY Delhi University Police Department at 607-746-4700. Application Instructions: To apply, please submit: Letter of interest Resume or Curriculum Vitae Contact information for three professional references Optional statement requested: SUNY Delhi is energized to lead the charge in developing a welcoming and intellectually diverse environment for all, a place where diversity, equity, and success guide our achievement, scholarship, character, and global citizenship. Please provide a short statement on your commitment to diversity and how you would incorporate it into this role. Campuses may consider a candidate's commitment to SUNY and/or the campus' mission and related values in hiring and promotion decisions, when relevant to position-specific knowledge, skills competencies, and experiences. This may include asking a job applicant to describe their commitment to and/or experience with diversity, equity, and inclusion (or any of SUNY's four pillars). Federal and state non-discrimination law require that higher education institutions do not offer employment opportunities based on a candidate's identity specific to race, sex, or national origin in the hiring process. For full consideration, please apply by October 20, 2026. Position will remain open until filled. SUNY Delhi is an AA/EOE employer. SUNY Delhi does not discriminate. Visa sponsorship is not available for this position. Your application will not be accepted if you require sponsorship to work in the United States. All people with disabilities are encouraged to apply Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation SUNY Delhi 454 Delhi Drive, Delhi, NY 13753"
